// Chapter 12, Section 12.8 — at most five delegations to the refunds agent
// per policy session in ten minutes, enforced at the orchestrator's Gateway.
//
// Syntax is the form measured in the author's October 2026 temporal-policy
// lab (count over ::request), adapted to an A2A passthrough target.
// The action id "refunds-agent___POST:/" is the one the Gateway generates for an A2A passthrough target named refunds-agent (live-tested 2026-11-11, CT-12-03). It stands for every JSON-RPC method sent to the target; a method such as tasks/get is context.input.method. Deploy in
// LOG_ONLY and read the decision log for the identifier the engine produces
// for A2A passthrough traffic.
//
// Lab findings that shape this policy:
//   * denied requests consumed a ::request limit in 40/40 trials; consider
//     counting ::response instead (untested);
//   * rotating the session id per call bypassed the limit (0/20 blocked);
//     the session id must be chosen by the backend at the entry point.

forbid (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"refunds-agent___POST:/",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-east-1:111122223333:gateway/example-gw"
)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long).
        (count for (t: Timepoint).
            where (formerly within 10m (AgentCore::Action::"refunds-agent___POST:/"::request{ eventResource: resource } && tp(t)))) == n
        && n > 5
};
